    "updated_at": "2023-06-02T09:22:47Z",
    "body": "Ah gotcha. I think this text at the start of [3.2](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#es-type-mapping) was probably meant to address that for conversions and most conversion-related algs:\r\n\r\n> Note that the sub-sections and algorithms below also apply to [annotated types](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#annotated-types) created by applying extended attributes to the types named in their headers.\r\n\r\n...which is kind of magical and yeah, it takes a very generous interpretation for that to make sense for the `BufferSource` algorithms at all (or even the conversions? the header text there is “Buffer source types” and `[AllowShared] Buffer source types` isn’t a thing, so it’s like a second layer of implicit expansions or something).",
